{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite","id":588752,"title":"What factors stop a spirit from powering a Rite?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-12T20:06:25-07:00","id":588752,"title":"What factors stop a spirit from powering a Rite?","content":"After reading the Silver Fang tribebook and seeing how in the fiction Albrecht's Pure Breed seemed to go up after his meeting with Fire Bird, it made me wonder why doesn't Fire Bird just power a Rite that allows Silver Fangs to gain Pure Breed. It would probably be something like the Shadow Lord's Rite of Conquest where a Shadow Lord can gain all sorts of huge Merits in exchange for taking on a suicidal quest. Should I assume that a Rite that purifies your Breed is something that already exists, but just wasn't mentioned in any of the books, and if not why wasn't the Rite ever created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:49:45-07:00","id":588807,"title":"","content":"There are a few totems that can increase Pure Breed by one dot. Offhand, I can only recall Suzaku from Stargazers Revised, though. As for a rite, it'd probably be rather costly, as you suggested. Perhaps not as demanding as the Rite of Conquest, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:55:41-07:00","id":589332,"title":"","content":"I don't think any spirit powers any rite solely. Not even incarnae. Rites are powered by the spirit world, meaning the spirits as a &quot;species&quot; or &quot;community&quot; power rites. In some cases a specific subgroup of the spirit as a species does, but not a single entity.<br /> <br /> From a rules standpoint, there don't need to be any spirits present (awaken or in Slumber) when a rite is enacted and it can still work. Nor have I ever read that spirits can or could have the power to sense when someone enacts a rite and choose to power it or not.<br /> <br /> From a setting standpoint there are limits even to godly beings like incarnae or Celestine spirits. One has to assume that there are some divine rules that limit their influence on the material world, or else there is no way to explain why basically immortal, omnipotent beings that are bent on destroying the world, like the urge wyrms have not simply materialised and brought upon the Apocalypse. Or why Helios and Luna haven't eradicated all evil.<br /> Point is that from a storytelling standpoint there might be ways to change the setting rather drastically, if you want to play such a game, but it is a huge effort and probably needs mortal agents to achieve such a goal. That is what stories are all about.<br /> <br /> That said, the Silver Fangs have a Rite, that leads a Silver Fang to a residence of a mate that is best suited to produce high pure breed offspring. It is not &quot;instant embodiment of Silver Fang-iness - just dance and chant&quot; but it is a way to keep the tribes high standards (if the mating takes place and isn't derailed by politics and such human pettiness).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T10:50:03-07:00","id":589358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=589332#post589332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From a rules standpoint, there don't need to be any spirits present (awaken or in Slumber) when a rite is enacted and it can still work. Nor have I ever read that spirits can or could have the power to sense when someone enacts a rite and choose to power it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there are rites that are powered by certain spirits and they can choose to power them or not. The punishment rite that allows a Garou to open a portal directly to Erebus is one such rite that used to specifically say that if the caster abuses the rite that the caster will pull them through the portal.<br /> <br /> It also used to be mentioned that when Garou try to enact the Caern building rite that it attracts all kinds of spirits, that is why it is not an endeavor taken lightly as it can inevitably draw the attention of Wyrm spirits. <br /> <br /> There also used to be a side note some where that said that Gaian Rites will no longer work once the caster has fallen to Wyrm, thus they need to learn the wyrmish version of the rite if one exists.<br /> <br /> To me this shows that spirits do empower the rites that Garou use and can choose not to power them if the Garou in question has done something that offends them or most likely breaks the oath the Garou have with Gaian spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:22:35-07:00","id":589405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=589358#post589358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually there are rites that are powered by certain spirits and they can choose to power them or not. The punishment rite that allows a Garou to open a portal directly to Erebus is one such rite that used to specifically say that if the caster abuses the rite that the caster will pull them through the portal.<br /> <br /> It also used to be mentioned that when Garou try to enact the Caern building rite that it attracts all kinds of spirits, that is why it is not an endeavor taken lightly as it can inevitably draw the attention of Wyrm spirits.<br /> <br /> There also used to be a side note some where that said that Gaian Rites will no longer work once the caster has fallen to Wyrm, thus they need to learn the wyrmish version of the rite if one exists.<br /> <br /> To me this shows that spirits do empower the rites that Garou use and can choose not to power them if the Garou in question has done something that offends them or most likely breaks the oath the Garou have with Gaian spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Gaian rites don't work in Malfeas, because there's nothing Gaian around, or if there is, it's immediately seized and carted off to be corrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T02:01:57-07:00","id":591022,"title":"","content":"... I suddenly see this little group of bane-goblins carting off spirit wisps from the Rite Master while cackling maniacally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T02:42:01-07:00","id":591030,"title":"","content":"1.Seize Gaia<br /> 2.????????<br /> 3. Profit!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T17:18:52-07:00","id":592106,"title":"","content":"Heh, heh... Underpants Bane...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T01:02:22-07:00","id":605387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=589358#post589358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually there are rites that are powered by certain spirits and they can choose to power them or not. The punishment rite that allows a Garou to open a portal directly to Erebus is one such rite that used to specifically say that if the caster abuses the rite that the caster will pull them through the portal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lady of Erebus teaches the Rite, that's true. But the ST is the arbiter to decide if the rite was used justly or not. I can't remember that this decision was to be made by the Lady, but could be made from neutral ST standpoint. Also, the Lady doesn't necessarily witness in a clairvoyant kind of way when the rite is enacted and lends it power or not. At least, this is not written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=589358#post589358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also used to be mentioned that when Garou try to enact the Caern building rite that it attracts all kinds of spirits, that is why it is not an endeavor taken lightly as it can inevitably draw the attention of Wyrm spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does, the Rite of summoning also calls a spirit. Hence my statement, that certain rites work, even when there isn't a spirit around - which is not the same as if I had stated &quot;rites have nothing to do with spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=589358#post589358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There also used to be a side note some where that said that Gaian Rites will no longer work once the caster has fallen to Wyrm, thus they need to learn the wyrmish version of the rite if one exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference for that ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=589358#post589358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me this shows that spirits do empower the rites that Garou use and can choose not to power them if the Garou in question has done something that offends them or most likely breaks the oath the Garou have with Gaian spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that spirits (as a people) empower rites, but not individual spirits. For individual spirits rarely have the Charms to perform the effect a rite would have. That said, one must be an shifter ans score successes to enact a rite - never read that spirits can choose that a Rite learned and performed correctly would not work. Is there a page reference to that ?<br /> <br /> Same for the Malfeas claim - is there a page reference for that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T07:37:04-07:00","id":605573,"title":"","content":"I was going to argue much of this (what heinrich wrote), but then got side tracked with life stuff. I do agree that spirits on the whole empower rites and not individual spirits.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=605387#post605387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Lady of Erebus teaches the Rite, that's true. But the ST is the arbiter to decide if the rite was used justly or not. I can't remember that this decision was to be made by the Lady, but could be made from neutral ST standpoint. Also, the Lady doesn't necessarily witness in a clairvoyant kind of way when the rite is enacted and lends it power or not. At least, this is not written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always viewed this as Charyss being an Incarna level spirit in her own Realm. The Elder Serpent of Pangea can probably do similar. They're plot device beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/588752-what-factors-stop-a-spirit-from-powering-a-rite?p=605387#post605387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Same for the Malfeas claim - is there a page reference for that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually looked this one up. Umbra Revised, page 74. It is odd, in that it's pretty much the only reference I've found to rites working this way. Since it's an odd line in a single book, I generally chalk it up to the writer. Wouldn't be the first time a writer wrote something odd that doesn't mesh well with the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}